Fix quit command prefix matching (issue #42; upstream bug, unfixed in v1.13
and on master).

In prot.c, which_cmd() matches command words with strncmp(), so any command
line beginning with "quit" (e.g. `quitgarbage\r\n` or `quit foo\r\n`) maps to
OP_QUIT. Unlike other commands, the OP_QUIT dispatch case validated nothing:
it set c->state = STATE_CLOSE and returned, silently closing the connection
with no response.

Single-word commands already guard against trailing garbage: the OP_STATS
case rejects lines whose length is not exactly CMD_STATS_LEN + 2 (\r\n
included) with BAD_FORMAT\r\n (e.g. `statsgarbage\r\n`). OP_QUIT lacked the
equivalent check.

Per the protocol specification (doc/protocol.txt), the command is exactly
`quit\r\n`; a malformed command line must yield BAD_FORMAT\r\n.

Add CMD_QUIT_LEN and the same trailing-garbage guard to the OP_QUIT case so
only the exact line `quit\r\n` closes the connection and malformed quit
prefixes return BAD_FORMAT\r\n.

--- a/prot.c
+++ b/prot.c
@@ -53,6 +53,8 @@
 
 #define CONSTSTRLEN(m) (sizeof(m) - 1)
 
+#define CMD_QUIT_LEN CONSTSTRLEN(CMD_QUIT)
+
 #define CMD_PEEK_READY_LEN CONSTSTRLEN(CMD_PEEK_READY)
 #define CMD_PEEK_DELAYED_LEN CONSTSTRLEN(CMD_PEEK_DELAYED)
 #define CMD_PEEK_BURIED_LEN CONSTSTRLEN(CMD_PEEK_BURIED)
@@ -1808,6 +1810,11 @@
         return;
 
     case OP_QUIT:
+        /* don't allow trailing garbage: only the exact line `quit` quits */
+        if (c->cmd_len != CMD_QUIT_LEN + 2) {
+            reply_msg(c, MSG_BAD_FORMAT);
+            return;
+        }
         c->state = STATE_CLOSE;
         return;
 
